# NEMESIS git hygiene

## No AI attribution

Never add `Co-Authored-By: Claude`, `Co-Authored-By: Anthropic`, "Generated with Claude Code",
or any AI attribution to commits, PRs, or docs in this repo. Strip if a harness re-adds them.
Before push: `git log` range must not contain those trailers.

## Push once green (overrides default "ask before push" for this project only)

When the user has asked for the work and verification is green:

1. `npx tsc` / desktop typecheck clean
2. Full vitest green (expect 550+ tests)
3. Build succeeds

…then **commit and push** to the feature branch without asking "should I push?".
Still: never commit secrets; review `git status`; never force-push `main`; prefer
`agent/nemesis-seven-hour-campaign` for NEMESIS work.

A red CI badge from **artifact storage quota** on upload steps is not automatically a code failure.
